config TEST_OSPI_FLASH_PERF
	bool "Enable OSPI flash performance test suite"
	default n
	help
	  Enable performance benchmarking test cases for the Alif OSPI flash
	  driver on the Zephyr test harness. When enabled, the build includes
	  the test suite defined in test_ospi_perf_tests.c, which performs
	  repeated erase/write/read operations across a bounded region of the
	  attached flash device (starting at the test region offset, never
	  offset 0). Each iteration measures elapsed time using k_uptime_get()
	  and accumulates totals so that average latency and throughput (KiB/s)
	  for erase, write, and read can be reported through LOG_INF. These
	  metrics help validate driver performance regressions and characterize
	  the OSPI bus at different clock speeds. Leave this disabled for
	  functional-only test runs as the performance suite extends execution
	  time significantly.

config TEST_OSPI_FLASH_FULL_CHIP
	bool "Enable the destructive full-chip OSPI flash perf test"
	depends on TEST_OSPI_FLASH_PERF
	default n
	help
	  Add a full-device erase/write/read case to the performance suite
	  (test_ospi_perf_full_chip). It calls flash_erase(0, total), which
	  uses the driver's chip-erase path and WIPES the entire device,
	  including offset 0 and any boot image stored there. Sized from DT
	  (num-of-sector x sector-size): 64 MiB on E7, 128 MiB on E8, so it
	  also runs for a long time. Keep this disabled in CI and only enable
	  it on a bring-up board that does not boot from this flash part.

config TEST_OSPI_FLASH_EXTRA
	bool "Enable extra OSPI flash API/DT suites"
	default n
	help
	  Build the extra flash-device, IRQ-routing, and XIP-transition suites.
	  Those tests use Zephyr flash APIs, HAL functions (prepare_transfer,
	  xip enable/disable), and user-configurable DT/Kconfig macros. They
	  do not read or write OSPI or AES registers from the testcase. If a
	  required driver or HAL API is missing or broken, the case fails.

config TEST_OSPI_XIP_LIVE
	bool "Dereference the XIP window in XIP API/transition suites"
	depends on TEST_OSPI_FLASH_EXTRA
	default y
	help
	  Allow the XIP transition and XIP API suites to read through the
	  memory-mapped XIP window after alif_hal_ospi_xip_enable(). This is
	  what turns the mapped-read, boundary-read and off-to-on cases into
	  real data comparisons.

	  A mapped read with a descriptor the attached device does not accept
	  is a bus fault rather than a failed assertion, so disable this option
	  on a board whose flash part or wiring differs from the one described
	  in devicetree. With it disabled those suites still run the HAL
	  enable/disable and flash_* half of each case and skip only the
	  window dereference.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
